; REQUEST-09 boundary under Phase 2.3 (nominal-per-instantiation): the collapsed-set instance is
; bound to a NAMED rule the author wrote (`named_set = set<key_hash>`, ident `NamedSet`). The binding
; becomes a transparent alias to the instantiation nominal — `pub type NamedSet = SetKeyHash;` — and
; the consumer's structural `[* key_hash]` (KeyHashList) request resolves via the nominal's OWN
; boundary class (own-produced), so generation SUCCEEDS. The pre-2.3 criterion-8 #3 hard error is
; deliberately retired: nominalization makes the shape structurally own-produced, so the collision
; that once required a rename/@name/drop no longer exists.
;
; The generic def carries the explicit `; @duplicates preserve` opt-out so the nominal keeps the plain
; `Vec`/`KeyHashList` boundary shape this fixture inspects — tag 258 now defaults to
; `@duplicates reject` (the well-known-tag registry), which would give the nominal an `OrderedSet`
; inner and a different boundary wrapper.
key_hash = bytes ; @newtype
set<a0> = #6.258([* a0]) / [* a0] ; @duplicates preserve
named_set = set<key_hash>
cert = [pool_owners: named_set]
